<article class="env-lemma" id="07AG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07AG">Lemma <span data-tag="07AG">35.12.3</span>.</a> Let $f : T \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. For any parasitic $\mathcal{O}$-module on $(\mathit{Sch}/T)_\tau $ the pushforward $f_*\mathcal{F}$ and the higher direct images $R^ if_*\mathcal{F}$ are parasitic $\mathcal{O}$-modules on $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_\tau $. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Recall that $R^ if_*\mathcal{F}$ is the sheaf associated to the presheaf 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  U \mapsto H^ i((\mathit{Sch}/U \times _ S T)_\tau , \mathcal{F})  \]
</div>
    <p>
       see Cohomology on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/072W" data-tag="072W">21.7.4</a>. If $U \to S$ is flat, then $U \times _ S T \to T$ is flat as a base change. Hence the displayed group is zero by Lemma <a href="/tag/0755" data-tag="0755">35.12.2</a>. If $\{ U_ i \to U\} $ is a $\tau $-covering then $U_ i \times _ S T \to T$ is also flat. Hence it is clear that the sheafification of the displayed presheaf is zero on schemes $U$ flat over $S$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>